answer = ('Method. For each network the currency list came from the Initialize logs of the PoolManager over its whole life where an endpoint served them, from the explorer holdings page where one answered, and from every token with a Transfer log naming the PoolManager inside the window. For every token balanceOf(PoolManager) was read at two blocks one day apart through Multicall3 with a block timestamp check, and all Transfer logs with the PoolManager as sender or recipient in between were summed. The 289 rows that failed were checked again: a second balance read by direct calls confirmed 287 of them, the logs were fetched again with an address filter for 282, and the two Arc rows were checked against the native balance. 1,262,679 token rows were tested. Scripts and raw results are in ' + W + '. '
          'Answer per network. ' + per_chain() + ' '
          'Classes and who can move them. Public trigger: sLGNS, sATH, sKLIMA on Polygon, sNVB and sSAC on BNB Smart Chain, USDI on Ethereum; any account can raise the balance inside one transaction, the balance does not fall back, and sync then settle, or take then repay, yields 8.78 sLGNS per epoch and 4,636.71 USDI today. On Polygon 661 sLGNS and 150 sATH rebases have already been taken as ERC-6909 claims. The surplus was never an accounted balance of any user. Scheduled multiplier set by the issuer: xStocks tokens on Ethereum, BNB Smart Chain, Monad and X Layer; SNDKx went up eightfold at a timestamp; no ordinary account can bracket it. Time formula upward: lending receipt tokens on twelve networks and 666, EXPT, EXPT2; no trigger, nothing to capture. Time formula downward, where the last to withdraw are locked: TURING on Ethereum, PYRE and SMK2 on Robinhood Chain, DDL on Arbitrum One. Rebase by a role: stETH, eETH, USDO, rUSDY, USD+ and USPD through the stETH rate. Second address of one ledger: EURe, the Frax custodian, POL at 0x1010, USDC on Arc. I found no token whose PoolManager balance an ordinary account can raise inside a transaction and that falls back later. '
          'Limits. Base, BNB Smart Chain and X Layer were tested for tokens active in the window only. 43 tokens on Robinhood Chain could not be read at old blocks. A token that changes balance less often than once a day passes this test unless the change fell inside the window.')
